Reconciled current `main` again at exact head `0383fa5a5bb35f72456ad65c9518b2f8502af40e` after the EvoLink registry entry landed:

- preserved this PR's `{PR_MERGE_DATE}` changelog entry at the top;
- retained the new EvoLink entry and all other current-main content;
- reran the focused registry suite (6/6) and `git diff --check` successfully.

The PR is mergeable. All eight substantive hosted checks are green; only the external Greptile review remains in progress.

Addressed the fail-closed review in exact head `ca8ec66`:

- non-string/unhashable document ids now return `unknown_doc` instead of raising from `dict.get`;
- both `resolve_span(["a"], ...)` and `span_gate(["a"], ...)` are covered;
- the span-gate docstring now states that empty and whitespace-only quotes fail closed.

Validation: all 28 tests passed against this checkout's `src` tree, and `git diff --check` passed. I have preserved the draft state pending your re-review.

Addressed the read-only override request in exact head `d6db3eb`:

- `--read-only` and `OPENTODO_READ_ONLY=1` now require a verified read-scoped token even when `--allow-full-token` is present;
- table-driven coverage proves both paths refuse before forwarding any MCP request;
- OpenSpec and user documentation now state that the full-token exception cannot weaken global read-only mode, and generated docs were refreshed.

Validation: `go test ./internal/cli`, `go vet ./...`, strict OpenSpec validation, docs build/check, and `git diff --check` passed. Marking the PR ready as requested.

Addressed the failing-locator issue in exact head `7c14eac` after merging current `master` (including #150):

- a locator parsed from the final error now takes precedence;
- a previously recorded locator is used only for a final locator/wait failure from `Locator` or `WaitEngine`;
- a caught optional-element timeout followed by an unrelated assertion now omits `failingLocator` instead of reporting the stale optional locator;
- the export fixture now represents a real final locator failure.

Validation: 6 focused failure-detail/export tests passed, then the full Maven suite passed 693/693; `git diff --check` passed. Marking the PR ready as requested.

